@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
# You can run these requests directly in VS Code by installing the "REST Client" extension (by Huachao Mao).
# Once installed, a small "Send Request" button will appear above each block.

### 1. Login to get token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "asha@corp.com",
    "password": "user123"
}

### Store the token from the response
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### 2. Get All Rooms
GET {{baseUrl}}/rooms
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Book Meeting A (Valid)
# @name bookMeetingA
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "Meeting A",
    "roomId": 1,
    "startTime": "2026-10-15 10:00:00",
    "endTime": "2026-10-15 11:00:00",
    "attendees": 4,
    "participantIds": [3, 4]
}

### Store Meeting A ID
@meetingA_id = {{bookMeetingA.response.body.data.meetingId}}

### 4. Book Meeting B (Conflict - Expect 409 Error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "Meeting B (Overlap)",
    "roomId": 1,
    "startTime": "2026-10-15 10:30:00",
    "endTime": "2026-10-15 11:30:00",
    "attendees": 4,
    "participantIds": []
}

### 5. Cancel Meeting A
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/meetings/{{meetingA_id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "reason": "Cancelled for testing"
}

### 6. Re-Book Meeting B (Now Valid because A was cancelled)
POST {{baseUrl}}/meetings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "title": "Meeting B (Overlap Resolved)",
    "roomId": 1,
    "startTime": "2026-10-15 10:30:00",
    "endTime": "2026-10-15 11:30:00",
    "attendees": 4,
    "participantIds": []
}

### 7. Test RoomBot AI
POST {{baseUrl}}/roombot/message
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
    "sessionId": "demo-chat-123",
    "text": "Book a room tomorrow at 3pm for 5 people"
}
